From decd0d0225e70e2fa5803550742b0980da04a74e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 21:38:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix AI service matching + add family notifications

- Fix root cause of matching silently failing: AI_SERVICE_URL pointed to
  localhost, which is unreachable from a separate Render service. Left a
  comment explaining the fix must be applied in the Render dashboard env
  vars, since that's what actually controls the deployed service.
- Add notification.service.js: sends email (Nodemailer/SMTP) and SMS
  (Twilio) to a missing person's contactInfo. Both channels are optional
  and independently configurable via env vars; missing config on one
  channel logs a warning instead of breaking the app.
- Wire notifications into match.controller.js's verifyMatch flow, so
  families are notified only after a human verifies a match (not on raw
  AI detection), to avoid false-positive distress. Match.notificationSent
  / notificationSentAt are now actually set.
- Add SMTP_*/TWILIO_* vars to .env.example.
- Add nodemailer + twilio to package.json.
